# dist-clone drives reconcile/dist-clone.sh against throwaway upstreams and consumers built under mktemp,
# and pins the SKILL.md sentences it implements (DCP). reconcile/emit-report.sh is declared because the
# fixture locates the reconcile directory by its presence (run.sh's `-f` test on it). Mutants are lone copies of
# dist-clone.sh, which resolves no sibling. The list is derived from run.sh's lib/preamble.sh source, that
# `-f` test, its `SUBJ="$RECON/dist-clone.sh"` line and its lib/mutant.sh source.
!core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/dist-clone.sh
!core/skills/ai-dlc-update/SKILL.md
core/skills/ai-dlc-update/reconcile/emit-report.sh
core/fixtures/lib/preamble.sh
core/fixtures/lib/mutant.sh
